1
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:07,939
(Night, Signal House)

2
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:14,320
I always thought I

3
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:18,160
was pretty good at observing people.

4
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:21,640
But I think you're even better
at it than I am.

5
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:23,400
You didn't even notice
I was watching you.

6
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:27,080
I think at the beginning,
you were observing too.

7
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:28,320
You sensed it?

8
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:30,280
I could feel it.

9
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,520
Like when we greeted each other.

10
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,240
Every time I did it,

11
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:39,000
I was always at this weird angle

12
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,160
when I greeted you, but...

13
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:40,960
You did it quietly.

14
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,480
Yeah, but every time I did that,

15
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:45,040
no matter what angle I was at,

16
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:46,880
when I looked at you and greeted you,

17
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,160
you always saw me.

18
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:49,880
And you would respond to me.

19
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:53,120
That's what I could feel.

20
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:56,560
What left the deepest impression on me

21
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:58,920
was the first day we entered the house.

22
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:00,000
You guys were sitting on the sofa.

23
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,600
Then I came up from the stairs.

24
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:04,019
(First day moving into Signal House)

25
00:01:04,019 --> 00:01:05,540
(Glances)

26
00:01:05,980 --> 00:01:07,860
(Eye contact)

27
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:14,600
When I reached the corner of the stairs,

28
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:16,560
I greeted you like this.

29
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:18,400
Yeah.

30
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:19,300
(Smiles)

31
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,760
You noticed me instantly.

32
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:29,760
If you weren't
intentionally paying attention,

33
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:33,040
I don't think you'd have noticed.

34
00:01:36,360 --> 00:01:37,160
Right?

35
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:39,000
Right?

36
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:46,100
(Nods)

37
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:50,840
Wanna go to the bubble pool?

38
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:51,760
The bubble pool?

39
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:53,000
The climbing one.

40
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:54,120
Let's go.

41
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:57,440
The two of us outside,

42
00:01:57,440 --> 00:01:58,600
chatting everywhere.

43
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:00,040
Yeah, let's go.

44
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:01,000
Immersive chatting.

45
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:04,960
Let's sit here.

46
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:05,480
Okay.

47
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:08,479
The spot you're sitting at

48
00:02:08,479 --> 00:02:10,039
is where I sent my texts.

49
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:13,280
This was the spot
I looked forward to every day.

50
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:14,120
Why?

51
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:15,300
(Asks)

52
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:18,560
Because I could send texts.

53
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:21,260
(Nods)

54
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:34,180
(Moves closer)

55
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:35,440
Did you open it?

56
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:36,240
I didn't dare.

57
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:38,440
But I'm planning to fix it later.

58
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:39,920
But do you need to change the medicine?

59
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:40,800
Yeah.

60
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:43,040
Yesterday he took that disinfectant...

61
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:44,640
The disinfectant.

62
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:45,200
Yeah, disinfect it.

63
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:45,560
Wrap it up.

64
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:46,200
Then wrap it up.

65
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:48,880
- Does it still hurt?
- Then he checked it.

66
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:49,480
Moved it around.

67
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,640
You should bend mine too then.

68
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:54,440
No.

69
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:57,120
Don't let both of us

70
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,600
go through the same pain.

71
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:00,640
That must hurt.

72
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:02,180
(Worried)

73
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:03,880
It hurts so much.

74
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,320
Take responsibility.

75
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:07,140
I'll take responsibility.

76
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:07,999
I'll be responsible till the end.

77
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:09,560
Responsible till the end.

78
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:13,580
(Hits)

79
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:14,640
Mosquito.

80
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:17,760
Don't bite me.

81
00:03:19,260 --> 00:03:20,620
(Glances)

82
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:23,800
What are you looking at?

83
00:03:25,820 --> 00:03:27,460
(Stares)

84
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:28,400
Beautiful.

85
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:30,360
You look pretty.

86
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:32,080
Here you go again with those lines.

87
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:34,200
You just say them so easily.

88
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:36,700
(Keeps staring)

89
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:37,720
Not saying anything anymore.

90
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:40,720
You're "scolding" me again.

91
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:44,480
Do you know what I'm about to say?

92
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:44,960
I know.

93
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:48,440
You're about to say it next.

94
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:50,320
(Laughs together)
What was I going to say?

95
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:52,680
Every time you say it,
I don't know what to do.

96
00:03:57,960 --> 00:03:59,720
We brought back some cake today.

97
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:00,440
Want some?

98
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:01,480
Yeah, I'll have a bite.

99
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:02,400
I want some.

100
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:04,240
Did you guys make the cake?

101
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:05,160
No, I bought it.

102
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:06,600
It's a really good cake.

103
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:08,040
It's just a little collapsed.

104
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:10,320
I thought you made it.

105
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:12,280
Then I guess I made it

106
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:13,080
a little ugly.

107
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:14,520
I'll have a small bite too.

108
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:15,760
This is matcha.

109
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:17,160
And there's yuzu inside.

110
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:18,079
You can dig into the middle.

111
00:04:18,079 --> 00:04:19,200
- There's filling inside.
- I'll take this side.

112
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:21,000
Yeah.

113
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,160
I'll take this bite.

114
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:23,440
Try some more from the inside.

115
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:24,480
This is the yuzu filling.

116
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:25,720
I'll have another bite.

117
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:26,560
You...

118
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:27,520
No, I can't eat anymore.

119
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:28,520
Seriously.

120
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:30,600
I've gained one kilogram after only
being in the house for a few days.

121
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:32,480
Here.

122
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:33,200
It's so good.

123
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:34,320
I'll scoop you a piece.

124
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:35,960
Okay, just a little.

125
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:38,200
You need to taste every layer.

126
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:39,040
Okay.

127
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:41,920
Thanks.

128
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:43,840
Chen Hewen

129
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:45,120
must've carried it

130
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:47,440
and tipped the box over.

131
00:04:48,460 --> 00:04:49,900
(Smiles)

132
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:53,800
Today, I...

133
00:04:58,720 --> 00:04:59,640
I was really brave.

134
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:03,520
I told Zhao Xilun,

135
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:05,760
"Let's be friends."

136
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:12,320
I feel like it was hard for him too.

137
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:15,720
I was like,

138
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:16,800
"This yuzu jam is so good."

139
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:17,920
I know.

140
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:19,640
My thoughts just jump around sometimes.

141
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,640
This yuzu jam is really good.

142
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:25,880
Yeah, have some more.

143
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:28,800
His dog even jumped
into the water today.

144
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:31,560
His dog is so well-behaved.

145
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:32,880
It looked so cute.

146
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:35,320
Super well-behaved.

147
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:36,120
Super cute.

148
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:38,680
Now you're making me
want to go on a date.

149
00:05:38,680 --> 00:05:39,840
I wanna see the dog.

150
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,880
Ask Zhao Xilun

151
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:43,040
if he can bring the dog over again.

152
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,040
I wanna see the dog too.

153
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:45,000
So cute.

154
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:03,880
I think I messed up the pattern.

155
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:06,560
This purple one doesn't belong here.

156
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:07,460
(Mumbling)

157
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:09,080
Grab a blue one.

158
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,480
I'm thinking about how to draw it.

159
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:21,840
(Making a moon for Sha Yue'er)
Quickly sketch it and I'll draw it.

160
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:23,520
I'll trace it. You sketch it first.

161
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:24,560
What kind of moon do you want?

162
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:25,520
Just a curved one.

163
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:26,240
I think that'll work.

164
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:26,960
A crescent moon.

165
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:28,500
Okay.

166
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:29,400
Do you understand what I mean?

167
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:30,800
It's okay. I have a way.

168
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:35,000
Impressive, Mr. Cao.

169
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,140
(Compliments)

170
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:43,000
So this is how you start the strokes.

171
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,640
I just filled it in completely earlier.

172
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:45,360
Yeah.

173
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:48,920
Then I'll make the outer curve rounder.

174
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:52,640
Sure, just trace the outline.

175
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:54,320
I'll color it.

176
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:59,880
I almost know how to draw now.

177
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:01,800
(Compliments)
That's amazing.

178
00:07:03,060 --> 00:07:05,580
(Laughs)

179
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,400
I can't tell if you're

180
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:08,760
being sarcastic anymore.

181
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:10,280
Of course I'm not.

182
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:14,080
It's good enough. Let's do it like this.

183
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,320
Trace it carefully on top.

184
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:17,760
Okay, I'll add two more lines.

185
00:07:17,760 --> 00:07:19,320
Let's use this one.

186
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:20,440
Okay.

187
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:21,800
On this side, right?

188
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:23,600
Yes, this is the frosted side.

189
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:26,320
Do you think we should adjust anything?

190
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:27,600
No, it's great.

191
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:28,600
Okay.

192
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:29,760
I'll draw it like this then.

193
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:30,560
Here.

194
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:38,840
It's done.

195
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:40,360
It's okay. We'll cut it out later.

196
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:47,080
But I think I drew it crooked.

197
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:48,920
It's okay.

198
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:50,680
I can even mess up tracing.

199
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:51,720
As long as it's drawn by you,

200
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:52,880
Sha Yue'er will probably be happy.

201
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:56,480
You're really good with words lately.

202
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:58,400
You've been studying.

203
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:03,360
You taught me well.

204
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:04,860
(Smiles)

205
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:08,000
When did I teach you that?

206
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:11,720
Looks good, right?

207
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:12,600
Yeah.

208
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:15,480
I was thinking, if we punch
a hole in the middle,

209
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:17,120
can the string go through?

210
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:17,920
A hole here.

211
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:19,880
Are you cutting it into a moon shape?

212
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:20,280
Yeah.

213
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:21,880
If we punch the hole first,

214
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:22,680
then cut it out,

215
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:24,200
the sides might become too thin.

216
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,160
It could break easily.

217
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:27,080
Then let's just cut it into a square.

218
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:29,960
Or we can try cutting it.

219
00:08:29,960 --> 00:08:31,040
If we make it into a strip,

220
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,159
it might actually look nice too.

221
00:08:32,159 --> 00:08:32,919
A moon.

222
00:08:32,919 --> 00:08:33,880
That works.

223
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:34,520
Yeah, think about it.

224
00:08:34,520 --> 00:08:37,480
A strip can't hang tilted like this.

225
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:39,159
It would have to hang vertically.

226
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:41,440
Okay.

227
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:42,320
You're so smart.

228
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:45,160
We can go out
and have fun again tomorrow.

229
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:47,920
I can finally go out with you.

230
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:50,960
It's only been a week
since we last went out.

231
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,440
Was yesterday fun?

232
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:55,400
It was.

233
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:58,000
Did you think it was fun?

234
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,360
It was.

235
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:02,400
How about this?

236
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:03,400
Not bad.

237
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:04,120
Amazing.

238
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:05,120
It's great. Let's go.

239
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:07,680
We can pack up soon.

240
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:10,800
Here, I'll blow it.

241
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:13,760
I'll blow it. I haven't
tried this before.

242
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:15,800
This is actually pretty dangerous.

243
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:16,690
Let me try.

244
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:18,160
(Acting cute)
Let me try.

245
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:20,520
Pull the string out first.

246
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:21,520
Then

247
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:22,760
press it. Yeah.

248
00:09:22,760 --> 00:09:24,740
(Heating tray)

249
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:27,760
Is it ready?

250
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:29,920
Of course not.

251
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:34,120
Of course not?

252
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:35,480
You need to be patient.

253
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:36,640
Blow on it slowly.

254
00:09:36,640 --> 00:09:37,520
Heat it slowly.

255
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:39,800
Is it ready?

256
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:40,520
Yeah, it is.

257
00:09:40,520 --> 00:09:41,280
Then I'll put it.

258
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:42,440
Blow.

259
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:47,600
Quick, save it.

260
00:09:49,040 --> 00:09:50,040
Keep blowing.

261
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:50,560
Don't stop.

262
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,080
Watch your hand.

263
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,120
Pause for a bit.

264
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:01,600
I'm better at drawing.

265
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:02,640
I'm not good at messing

266
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:03,200
with this.

267
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:07,240
Melt it a little more with the heat.

268
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:11,280
That's it. It's okay.

269
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:13,840
Look, it's heart-shaped.

270
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:14,360
Let's go.

271
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:14,840
Okay.

272
00:10:15,920 --> 00:10:16,560
Let's go.

273
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:22,240
We made you a shrink plastic,

274
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:23,200
but we messed it up while heating it.

275
00:10:23,560 --> 00:10:25,280
It's okay.

276
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:26,580
I like it.

277
00:10:26,580 --> 00:10:27,660
We'll make you another one
when we get back.

278
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:29,480
It got crooked.

279
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:33,280
A blue moon.

280
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:34,440
It has such a textured look.

281
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:35,040
So much texture.

282
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:36,280
It feels like the moon
is reflected in water.

283
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:36,800
Yeah.

284
00:10:37,560 --> 00:10:38,520
It's really beautiful.

285
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:39,240
Keep it.

286
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:40,960
Love you.

287
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:48,580
(Mutual date, Cui Kaiyi and Cao Yiheng)

288
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:56,320
Can these be made

289
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:56,760
